Trusted Research Environment (TRE) Policy-as-Code Project Playbook
1. Project Overview & Objectives
This playbook provides a step-by-step operational guide for implementing, deploying, and maintaining a machine-readable, graph-navigable Policy-as-Code (PaC) platform for Trusted Research Environments (TRE) / Secure Data Environments (SDE).
Key Goals:
* Semantic Transparency: Build an auditable OWL 2 / RDF ontology mapping clinical data governance, hospital operational tiers, and research project access (aligned with the Five Safes Framework and SATRE pillars).
* Deterministic Enforcement: Resolve the Open-World Assumption (OWA) into Closed-World Assumption (CWA) security checks via SHACL shapes and compile them into low-latency Open Policy Agent (OPA) Rego rules.
* Dual-Persona Public Portal: Expose a clean, plain-English Governance Atlas alongside an interactive Cytoscape knowledge graph viewer for researchers, auditors, and the public.
* AI & MCP Governance: Incorporate EU AI Act risk tiers and Model Context Protocol (MCP) tool-use boundaries for autonomous analytics agents.


