3. Implementation Roadmap & Phases
Phase 1: Knowledge Modeling & Baseline Ontology (Weeks 1–4)
* Define Scope: Distinguish Policy Metadata (roles, data tiers, retention limits) from Runtime State (active pods, network connections).
* Ontology Authoring: Build modular Turtle (.ttl) definitions covering:
   * Five Safes: Safe Person, Safe Project, Safe Setting, Safe Data, Safe Output.
   * SATRE Pillars: Information Governance, Computing Infrastructure, Data Management, Software Operations.
   * Quantitative SDC: Primary cell suppression ($k \ge 10$) and dominance rules ($k% \le 80%$).
   * AI Governance: EU AI Act risk categorization and Model Context Protocol (MCP) tool bounds (mcp:ExecuteSQL, mcp:ExportSummary).
* GitOps Setup: Establish a version-controlled repository with semantic linting tools (pyshacl, rdfpipe) in CI.
Phase 2: Validation Logic & Graph Test Suite (Weeks 5–8)
* SHACL Shapes: Formalize policies into SHACL node and property shapes for deterministic pass/fail outcomes.
* Test Fixtures: Construct unit test graphs for positive cases (accredited researcher, active ethics, egress-disabled enclave) and negative cases (expired IG training, un-isolated subnets).
* Automated Testing: Run pytest harness (tests/test_shapes.py) to validate graphs against constraints in CI.
Phase 3: Public Documentation & Exploration Interface (Weeks 9–12)
* Automated Documentation: Run compiler/generate_docs.py to extract governance metadata into GOVERNANCE_CHARTER.md for Trust boards and Freedom of Information (FOI) requests.
* Dual-Persona Web Portal: Deploy the static web UI (web/index.html) featuring:
   * Plain-English Governance Atlas: High-level cards and compliance summaries for public visitors and clinical staff.
   * Interactive Graph Explorer: Cytoscape.js rendering of OWL classes, properties, and MCP tool relationships with sidebar inspectors.
* Static Deployment: Publish compiled assets to GitHub Pages or cloud static storage via CI/CD workflows.
Phase 4: Runtime Enforcement Integration (Weeks 13–16)
* OPA Compilation: Execute compiler/rdf_to_rego.py to translate semantic Turtle definitions and SDC thresholds into executable Open Policy Agent (OPA) Rego rules.
* Policy Enforcement Points (PEP):
   * Workspace Admission: Integrate OPA with Kubernetes admission controllers or API gateways to intercept workspace provisioning.
   * Network & Egress Controls: Enforce enclave isolation and automate airlock egress reviews using quantitative SHACL/SDC checks.
   * Audit Lineage: Emit W3C PROV-O RDF triples on every major event (project provisioned, access revoked, egress granted) to an append-only audit log.


